~ start

Mother: Okay, everyone, quiet! Quiet! Light the candle!
Father: Make a wish, anak. Make it a good one.
Ollie: Hmm... okay. I know what I want.
Mother: Don't say it out loud, or it won't come true!
Ollie: I wasn't going to!
Sibling: Hurry up, Kuya! I want cake!

Ollie takes a deep breath. The candle flickers.

Ollie: Happy birthday to me...

[wait=0.8]

Outside, the rain thickens. A low rumble rolls under the floorboards.

Father: ...Did you hear that?
Mother: It's just thunder, dear.
Father: [speed=0.6]That wasn't thunder.[/speed]

The candle goes out. Not from Ollie's breath.

Ollie: Papa? Why is the floor wet?

Water creeps across the tiles, thin and dark, slipping around everyone's feet.

Sibling: Mama, it's cold...
Mother: [shake rate=15 level=5]Oh no. Oh no, no...[/shake]

Father: [shake rate=22 level=8]Everyone, listen to me![/shake]
Father: The river broke through. We don't have much time.

Ollie: But... the cake. It's my birthday.
Father: I know, anak. I know. [wait=0.6] I'm sorry.

Father: [shake rate=20 level=7]Gather your things, now! Only what you can carry![/shake]
Father: Documents, flashlight, water, phone. Nothing else!
Mother: [shake rate=18 level=6]Come, come, stay close to me![/shake]

Ollie: Papa, what about our house?
Father: Houses can be rebuilt. [wait=0.8] You can't. Move!

The rumble grows louder. Somewhere beyond the walls, something gives way.

Sibling: [shake rate=25 level=9]Kuya, I'm scared![/shake]
Ollie: Hold my hand. Don't let go, okay? Not for anything.

Ollie glances back at the table. The cake sits untouched, a single wax stream frozen down the side.

Ollie: ...So much for my wish.

Father: [shake rate=30 level=12]OLLIE! NOW![/shake]

=> END